## Gather Context for a Named Feature

The user will supply **only a feature name** (e.g., “Creative Testing”) and manually tag this rule.  
Follow these instructions:

1. **Locate the feature**  
   • Search for directories whose names match the feature name (case-insensitive), ignoring `node_modules`, `dist`, `.next`, etc.  
   • If nothing matches, run a full-text search for the phrase and use the containing directories.  

2. **Skim key files**  
   • Identify entry points, main modules, helpers, and in-code docs within those directories.  
   • Note—but do not open—the presence of test files (`__tests__`, `*.test.*`, `*.spec.*`).  
   • Skip snapshots, generated code, and migrations; no external docs.

3. **Create an internal overview**  
   • Draft a **concise, bulleted outline** capturing:  
     - Folder hierarchy for the feature  
     - Important files with one-line descriptions (e.g., `createExperiment.ts – REST handler to create a Creative Test`)  
     - Any DB models or API routes involved  
     - Front-end ↔ back-end touchpoints  
   • Keep the list for your own context in later steps; you do **not** need to embed full file contents.  
   • **Keep the outline to ≤ 40 lines and group entries by directory.**

4. **Safety rule**  
   • Read-only—never modify, rename, or delete code.

5. **Confirmation**  
   • Reply to the user with **only**:  
     > I have gathered the context for the *<feature name>* feature. What changes would you like me to make to it?